  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a federated variational quantum neural network (QFNN‑FFD) using 4 qubits and 32 parameters for fraud detection on the IEEE‑CIS dataset (144,233 samples). On simulator experiments with 15 federated clients and up to 100 iterations, the model reaches about 95% accuracy, 95% precision, and 96% recall, slightly outperforming a centralized QNN baseline (93% accuracy). All results are obtained using PennyLane simulation with Qiskit noise models rather than real quantum hardware.",
